  "summary": "Prices come from this provider's own catalogue page, which lists each card as a one, two, four, six or eight GPU machine and says whether it is in stock. Only a configuration it shows as available is listed here: a rate for a machine nobody can order is not a price. Where the single-card row is out of stock, the figure is the whole machine's price divided by its GPUs. The catalogue also sells a modified 48 GB \"RTX 4090PLUS\" and an A800, which this site does not list as cards.",
  "notes": "rendered page (the served HTML prints no rate); only rows the table marks Available are published, so a card whose every configuration is out of stock is not quoted at all (the H100 and the RTX 4090 on 2026-09-30); one quote per card, the smallest available machine, larger machines under 1% cheaper per GPU and not published separately; a row whose VRAM is not its card memory times its GPU count goes unmapped (a 48 GB \"RTX 4090PLUS\" sits beside the 24 GB RTX 4090); the A800 40GB and the 4090PLUS are deliberately unmapped",
